  "notes": [
    "The LP-fee pot's MIC was sold by the contract into the thin MIC/WBNB pair (the anchor's 179 MIC was over 40% of that pool's MIC), so per rule 12 the loss is the USDT the pot paid to claimers other than the fee wallets in the anchor and campaign, less the 0.35% LP fee the claimers' own in-tx buys added to the pot.",
    "The campaign is every tx with swapAndSendLPFeeEvent: no LP fee was paid before the anchor. The mid-January MIC/USDT pool collapse came from ordinary router sells, not swapManual, and is not counted."
